  tags: ['Pipeline', 'UDIM', 'Substance', 'UE5'],\nsrc/components/CVPage.jsx:227:    brand: 'Houdini · UE5',\nsrc/components/CVPage.jsx:231:    tags: ['Houdini', 'Level Design', 'PCG', 'Heightfield'],\nsrc/components/CVPage.jsx:235:    title: 'Procedural Grass System',\nsrc/components/CVPage.jsx:236:    brand: 'Houdini · Substance · UE5',\nsrc/components/CVPage.jsx:240:    tags: ['Houdini', 'Substance', 'VAT', 'Vegetation'],\nsrc/components/CVPage.jsx:245:    brand: 'Unreal Engine 5',\nsrc/components/CVPage.jsx:262:    title: 'Louisiana Bayou V1.5',\nsrc/components/CVPage.jsx:263:    brand: 'Unreal Engine 5',\nsrc/components/CVPage.jsx:272:    brand: 'Substance Designer',\nsrc/components/CVPage.jsx:274:    descriptionEn: 'Procedural sedimentary rock material. Erosion, cracks, color variation. Custom sub-graphs, chunk breakup, fuzzy edges. 4K.',\nsrc/components/CVPage.jsx:276:    tags: ['Substance', 'Procedural', 'Texturing'],\nsrc/components/CVPage.jsx:280:    title: 'Substance Designer MCP Plugin',\nsrc/components/CVPage.jsx:282:    description: 'Plugin MCP pour Substance Designer. Description en langage naturel -> graphe PBR complet et fonctionnel. Open source.',\nsrc/components/CVPage.jsx:283:    descriptionEn: 'MCP plugin for Substance Designer. Natural language → complete functional PBR graph. Open source.',\nsrc/components/CVPage.jsx:285:    tags: ['MCP', 'Python', 'AI', 'Substance', 'Open Source'],\nsrc/components/CVPage.jsx:290:    brand: 'C++ · Unreal Engine 5',\nsrc/components/CVPage.jsx:299:    brand: 'Unreal Engine 5',\nsrc/components/CVPage.jsx:317:    brand: 'Houdini',\nsrc/components/CVPage.jsx:319:    descriptionEn: 'Procedural water wheel geometry + FLIP water simulation. Parametric: size, bucket count, wood aging, moss growth.',\nsrc/components/CVPage.jsx:321:    tags: ['Houdini', 'FLIP', 'Procedural', 'Simulation'],\nsrc/components/CVPage.jsx:325:    title: 'Pampa Grass HDA',\nsrc/components/CVPage.jsx:326:    brand: 'Houdini HDA · UE5',\nsrc/components/CVPage.jsx:330:    tags: ['Houdini', 'VEX', 'HDA', 'Vegetation', 'UE5'],\nsrc/components/CVPage.jsx:428:    ? 'Technical Artist specializing in Houdini + Unreal Engine 5. From procedural modeling to pipeline architecture - I design t…2710 tokens truncated…purement artistique. Je bake les mesh maps en 4K directement dans Substance Painter, en sautant intentionnellement la phase high-poly ZBrush. Pour les props architecturaux standard, un bake low-poly propre combine a des materiaux PBR haute qualite est tres efficace et economise des heures de production.\"\nsrc/projectSlides.jsx:972:            \"Using Black Masks and procedural generators (Dirt, Position, Curvature), I paint specific areas that need wear, moisture, and aging. Substance Painter is built for exactly this level of bespoke, granular artistic control.\",\nsrc/projectSlides.jsx:973:            \"En utilisant des Black Masks et des generateurs proceduraux (Dirt, Position, Curvature), je peins les zones specifiques qui necessitent usure, humidite et vieillissement. Substance Painter est concu exactement pour ce niveau de controle artistique granulaire et sur mesure.\"\nsrc/projectSlides.jsx:985:              {imgZoom(\"sp-dirt-layer-stack.webp\", \"Substance Painter layer stack with Dirt generator, Warp filter, and mask hierarchy\", \"right\")}\nsrc/projectSlides.jsx:1003:            {captionBelow(t(\"Custom name automation for Substance Painter and Unreal Engine convention\", \"Automatisation du nommage pour la convention Substance Painter et Unreal Engine\"))}\nsrc/projectSlides.jsx:1020:            \"The textures are packed and exported as BaseColor (BC), ORM, and Normal (N) maps across 2048x2048 UDIM tiles. In Unreal Engine, Virtual Texturing must be enabled for UDIM support. The Master Material (M_Master_BC_ORM_N) uses Virtual Texture Parameters with correctly assigned Sampler Types: Virtual Color for BaseColor, Virtual Normal for the Normal map, and Linear Color for the ORM.\",\nsrc/projectSlides.jsx:1021:            \"Les textures sont packees et exportees en maps BaseColor (BC), ORM et Normal (N) sur des tiles UDIM 2048x2048. Dans Unreal Engine, le Virtual Texturing doit etre active pour le support UDIM. Le Master Material (M_Master_BC_ORM_N) utilise des Virtual Texture Parameters avec les Sampler Types correctement assignes : Virtual Color pour le BaseColor, Virtual Normal pour la Normal map, et Linear Color pour l'ORM.\"\nsrc/projectSlides.jsx:1026:          {captionBelow(t(\"In Unreal, beware to be on Virtual Color and Virtual Normal - wrong Sampler Types will break the material silently\", \"Dans Unreal, attention a etre sur Virtual Color et Virtual Normal - de mauvais Sampler Types casseront le materiau silencieusement\"))}\nsrc/projectSlides.jsx:1038:            \"Procedural Repair \\u00b7 Automated UDIMs \\u00b7 Virtual Textures\",\nsrc/projectSlides.jsx:1039:            \"Reparation Procedurale \\u00b7 UDIMs Automatises \\u00b7 Virtual Textures\"\nsrc/projectSlides.jsx:1044:            <SmartImg src={`${MS_BASE}/ue-result-front.webp`} alt=\"Final result in Unreal Engine\" loading=\"lazy\" style={{ width: \"100%\", height: \"100%\", objectFit: \"cover\", display: \"block\", cursor: \"zoom-in\" }} onClick={() => setViewerSrc(`${MS_BASE}/ue-result-front.webp`)} />\nsrc/projectSlides.jsx:1047:            <SmartImg src={`${MS_BASE}/ue-result-top.webp`} alt=\"Final result in Unreal Engine\" loading=\"lazy\" style={{ width: \"100%\", height: \"100%\", objectFit: \"cover\", display: \"block\", cursor: \"zoom-in\" }} onClick={() => setViewerSrc(`${MS_BASE}/ue-result-top.webp`)} />\nsrc/projectSlides.jsx:1050:        {captionBelow(t(\"Final result in Unreal Engine\", \"Resultat final dans Unreal Engine\"))}\nsrc/projectSlides.jsx:1057:        {eyebrow(t(\"Unreal Render\", \"Rendu Unreal\"))}\nsrc/projectSlides.jsx:1060:          {imgZoom(\"unreal-render-final.webp\", \"Final Unreal Engine render after Photoshop compositing\")}\nsrc/projectSlides.jsx:1072:            {[\"Houdini\", \"RizomUV\", \"Substance Designer\", \"Substance Painter\", \"Unreal Engine 5\"].flatMap((tool, j) => [\nsrc/projectSlides.jsx:1099:   From Unreal PCG to Houdini HDA\nsrc/projectSlides.jsx:1211:              From Unreal PCG to Houdini HDA\nsrc/projectSlides.jsx:1216:              \"I built a new system handled with Houdini HDA because I was struggling with PCG in Unreal. My PC was frequently hitting low memory pressure, and it was taking a lot of time to set up and create multiple setups for every system of my environment - especially since Blueprints + PCG is still very laggy on my laptop.\",\nsrc/projectSlides.jsx:1217:              \"J'ai construit un nouveau système géré avec un HDA Houdini parce que je galérais avec le PCG dans Unreal. Mon PC tombait fréquemment en low memory pressure, et ça prenait beaucoup de temps pour configurer chaque système de mon environnement - d'autant plus que Blueprints + PCG reste très lent sur mon laptop.\"\nsrc/projectSlides.jsx:1228:        {/* ── HERO IMAGE - From Houdini to Unreal ── */}\nsrc/projectSlides.jsx:1230:          {imgZoom(\"hero-houdini-to-unreal.webp\", \"From Houdini to Unreal - Full HDA Level Design\")}\nsrc/projectSlides.jsx:1242:            }}>From Houdini to Unreal in One HDA</p>\nsrc/projectSlides.jsx:1248:              \"Package all your Level Design and blockout into a single Houdini Digital Asset.\",\nsrc/projectSlides.jsx:1249:              \"Regroupez tout votre Level Design et blockout dans un seul Houdini Digital Asset.\"\nsrc/projectSlides.jsx:1263:            \"The complete scene blockout in Houdini's viewport. All assets are placed and scattered procedurally on the heightfield terrain - trees, vegetation, hero props, and the church house.\",\nsrc/projectSlides.jsx:1264:            \"Le blockout complet de la scène dans le viewport Houdini. Tous les assets sont placés et scatterés procéduralement sur le terrain heightfield - arbres, végétation, props hero, et la church house.\"\nsrc/projectSlides.jsx:1268:          {imgZoom(\"houdini-full-blockout.webp\", \"Houdini Full Blockout\", { mask: \"right\" })}\nsrc/projectSlides.jsx:1277:        {h2(t(\"Import HDA in Unreal\", \"Import du HDA dans Unreal\"))}\nsrc/projectSlides.jsx:1280:            \"The Houdini Digital Asset is imported directly into Unreal Engine. Once cooked, every element from the HDA is available as individual actors in the scene - fully editable and ready for material assignment.\",\nsrc/projectSlides.jsx:1281:            \"Le Houdini Digital Asset est importé directement dans Unreal Engine. Une fois cuit, chaque élément du HDA est disponible en tant qu'acteur individuel dans la scène - entièrement éditable et prêt pour l'assignation de matériaux.\"\nsrc/projectSlides.jsx:1285:          {imgZoom(\"import-hda-unreal.webp\", \"Import HDA in Unreal Engine\", { mask: \"left\" })}\nsrc/projectSlides.jsx:1420:            The better approach: bake an <strong style={{ color: \"#fff\" }}>opacity mask</strong> from the Heightfield Output (8-bit, red channel only), plug it into your Water Shader, and enable <strong style={{ color: \"#fff\" }}>Dither Temporal AA</strong> in Unreal.\nsrc/projectSlides.jsx:1423:            La meilleure approche : baker un <strong style={{ color: \"#fff\" }}>masque d'opacité</strong> depuis le Heightfield Output (8-bit, canal rouge uniquement), le brancher dans votre Water Shader, et activer <strong style={{ color: \"#fff\" }}>Dither Temporal AA</strong> dans Unreal.\nsrc/projectSlides.jsx:1445:          {imgZoom(\"softened-water-shader.webp\", \"Softened water borders in Unreal\")}\nsrc/projectSlides.jsx:1480:            \"Heightfield Scatter distributes vegetation across the terrain using mask layers. Grass is scattered first, then palmettos reuse the same point cloud at a lower density, and trees get their own dedicated scatter pass.\",\nsrc/projectSlides.jsx:1496:            { file: \"heightfield-scatter-grass.webp\", label: t(\"Heightfield Scatter\", \"Heightfield Scatter\"), sub: t(\"Grass and base vegetation\", \"Herbe et végétation de base\") },\nsrc/projectSlides.jsx:1550:            \"The 4 hero assets and all scattered vegetation are merged into a single output, then packaged as one Houdini Digital Asset. One file, one import, one cook - your entire level design in a single node.\",\nsrc/projectSlides.jsx:1551:            \"Les 4 assets hero et toute la végétation scatterée sont fusionnés en une seule sortie, puis packagés en un seul Houdini Digital Asset. Un fichier, un import, un cook - tout votre level design dans un seul nœud.\"\nsrc/projectSlides.jsx:1584:            { src: `${AS_BASE}/unreal-import-hda.webp`, label: t(\"Unreal Import HDA\", \"Import HDA dans Unreal\"), sub: t(\"Full scene cooked\", \"Scène complète cuite\") },\nsrc/projectSlides.jsx:1636:            <>If you use <strong style={{ color: \"#fff\" }}>Pack</strong> nodes before merging your assets, you can cook your HDA in Unreal and still keep your static meshes as individual assets. Incredibly convenient for texturing later on - each mesh gets its own material slot, just like importing FBX or OBJ files.</>,\nsrc/projectSlides.jsx:1637:            <>Si vous utilisez les nœuds <strong style={{ color: \"#fff\" }}>Pack</strong> avant de fusionner vos assets, vous pouvez cuire votre HDA dans Unreal tout en gardant vos static meshes en tant qu'assets individuels. Extrêmement pratique pour le texturing par la suite - chaque mesh obtient son propre slot de matériau, comme pour un import FBX ou OBJ.</>\nsrc/projectSlides.jsx:1643:            \"Unreal Content Browser - individual static meshes baked from the HDA, ready for material assignment\",\nsrc/projectSlides.jsx:1644:            \"Unreal Content Browser - static meshes individuels bakés depuis le HDA, prêts pour l'assignation de matériaux\"\nsrc/projectSlides.jsx:1678:function LouisianaBayouChurchSlides({ isMobile, lang }) {\nsrc/projectSlides.jsx:1872:            alt=\"Louisiana Bayou Church\"\nsrc/projectSlides.jsx:1934:              Louisiana<br />Bayou<br />Church\nsrc/projectSlides.jsx:2014:            alt=\"Louisiana Bayou Church Modeling\"\nsrc/projectSlides.jsx:2063:            Louisiana Bayou Church<br />\nsrc/projectSlides.jsx:2065:              {t(\"A Procedural Component System in Houdini\", \"Un Système de Composants Procédural dans Houdini\")}\nsrc/projectSlides.jsx:2070:              \"A small wooden church, modeled in Houdini. Style from Red Dead Redemption II. Rural chapel, plain siding, shingled roof, a cross at the gable.\",\nsrc/projectSlides.jsx:2071:              \"Une petite église en bois, modélisée dans Houdini. Style emprunté à Red Dead Redemption II. Chapelle rurale, bardage simple, toit en bardeaux, une croix au pignon.\"\nsrc/projectSlides.jsx:2499:              Houdini · Church\nsrc/projectSlides.jsx:2504:                \"A procedural staircase HDA for the Louisiana Bayou Church.\",\nsrc/projectSlides.jsx:2505:                \"Un escalier procedural en HDA pour la Louisiana Bayou Church.\"\nsrc/projectSlides.jsx:2666:            <p style={{ fontFamily: \"'AnthropicMono', 'ui-monospace', monospace\", fontWeight: 500, fontSize: isMobile ? \"0.64rem\" : \"0.7rem\", letterSpacing: \"0.52em\", textTransform: \"uppercase\", color: \"rgba(255,255,255,0.45)\", margin: \"0 0 20px 0\" }}>Houdini</p>\nsrc/projectSlides.jsx:2669:              {t(\"How to get varied planks without multi-UDIM. A procedural UV approach in Houdini.\", \"Comment avoir des planches variées sans multi-UDIM. Une approche UV procédurale dans Houdini.\")}\nsrc/projectSlides.jsx:2700:            \"Disclaimer: this method is not the definitive solution, but it does allow in Houdini to repeat a mesh with a varied texture.\",\nsrc/projectSlides.jsx:2701:            \"Disclaimer : cette méthode n'est pas l'alpha et l'oméga, elle permet néanmoins dans Houdini d'avoir une répétition d'un mesh avec une texture variée.\"\nsrc/projectSlides.jsx:2714:            \"I installed RizomUV, but I quickly realized that for a repeatable tileable surface, RizomUV was not the right solution and was more suited to unique surfaces, especially since it creates a proxy, which is not ideal when working inside Houdini. I then tried to focus on UV Unwrap and UV Layout nodes placed before Copy to Points, because I told myself that if the UVs were computed beforehand, I could then distribute a more relevant 0-1 space across each copy.\",\nsrc/projectSlides.jsx:2715:            \"J'ai installé RizomUV, mais je me suis rendu compte que pour une surface tileable répétable, RizomUV n'était pas la solution et était plus dédié aux surfaces uniques, sachant qu'il crée un proxy, ce qui n'est pas idéal en travaillant dans Houdini. J'ai ensuite essayé de me concentrer autour des nodes UV Unwrap et UV Layout placés avant le Copy to Points, car je me suis dit que si les UVs étaient calculés auparavant, je pourrais ensuite distribuer un espace 0-1 plus pertinent sur chaque copie.\"\nsrc/projectSlides.jsx:2727:          {imgZoom(\"graph.webp\", \"Houdini graph\")}\nsrc/projectSlides.jsx:2767:              {t(\"One mesh. Procedural naming. Infinite variations.\", \"Un mesh. Naming procédural. Variations infinies.\")}\nsrc/projectSlides.jsx:2778:        {h2(t(\"Procedural UV Offset.\", \"Procedural UV Offset.\"))}\nsrc/projectSlides.jsx:2791:              [t(\"V1: Manual\", \"V1: Manuel\"), t(\"V2: Procedural\", \"V2: Procédural\")],\nsrc/projectSlides.jsx:2889:          {imgZoom(\"graph-comparison.webp\", \"Houdini graph old vs new\")}\nsrc/projectSlides.jsx:2893:        <p style={{ fontFamily: \"'AnthropicMono', 'ui-monospace', monospace\", fontSize: \"0.65rem\", letterSpacing: \"0.2em\", textTransform: \"uppercase\", color: \"rgba(255,255,255,0.3)\", margin: \"14px 0 0\" }}>Houdini Graph</p>\nsrc/projectSlides.jsx:2911:        {h2(t(\"Procedural UV Offset.\", \"Procedural UV Offset.\"))}\nsrc/projectSlides.jsx:3090:function LouisianaBayouSlides({ isMobile, lang }) {\nsrc/projectSlides.jsx:3101:          {imgZoom(\"thumbnail.webp\", \"Louisiana Bayou V1.5\", { mask: \"left\" })}\nsrc/projectSlides.jsx:3103:        <h1 style={titleStyle}>{t(\"Louisiana Bayou V1.5\", \"Louisiana Bayou V1.5\")}</h1>\nsrc/projectSlides.jsx:3105:          \"A major technical update to the atmospheric environment project. Pushing deeper into UE5 rendering systems to bring a Louisiana swamp to life. The scene centers on an isolated wooden house half-submerged in bayou water, surrounded by towering swamp cypress trees draped in Spanish moss.\",\nsrc/projectSlides.jsx:3127:          {captionBelow(t(\"Latest render of the bayou scene in Unreal Engine 5\", \"Dernier rendu de la scene du bayou dans Unreal Engine 5\"))}\nsrc/projectSlides.jsx:3192:          \"This project was born from an inspiration after watching the movie Sinners. I was immersed by the atmosphere and wanted to dive into the visual history of Louisiana.\",\nsrc/projectSlides.jsx:3254:          \"Procedural cliff material created entirely in Substance Designer. Layered sedimentary rock with realistic erosion, cracks, and color variation. Built from scratch using custom subgraphs for tile layers, chunk breakup, and fuzzy edge detail at 4K resolution.\",\nsrc/projectSlides.jsx:3255:          \"Materiau de falaise procedural entierement realise dans Substance Designer. Roche sedimentaire stratifiee avec erosion, fissures et variation de couleur. Construit de zero avec des sous-graphes custom en resolution 4K.\"\nsrc/projectSlides.jsx:3366:          {imgZoom(\"thumbnail.webp\", \"Substance Designer MCP Plugin\", { mask: \"left\" })}\nsrc/projectSlides.jsx:3368:        <h1 style={titleStyle}>{t(\"Substance Designer MCP Plugin\", \"Plugin MCP Substance Designer\")}</h1>\nsrc/projectSlides.jsx:3370:          \"Describe a material in plain English and get a complete, working PBR graph inside Substance Designer. Built for technical artists who want to move faster without giving up control over the result. The agent handles the structure, you own the craft.\",\nsrc/projectSlides.jsx:3371:          \"Decrivez un materiau en langage naturel, obtenez un graphe PBR complet et fonctionnel dans Substance Designer. Concu pour les artistes techniques. L'agent gere la structure, vous maitrisez le savoir-faire.\"\nsrc/projectSlides.jsx:3417:          \"First Substance Designer fabric material study. Ornate woven pattern with procedural thread structure, weave variation, and surface relief. Built entirely from scratch: fiber direction, interlace logic, color variation per thread, and micro-detail normal pass.\",\nsrc/projectSlides.jsx:3418:          \"Premiere etude de materiau tissu dans Substance Designer. Motif tisse orne avec structure de fil procedurale, variation de tissage et relief de surface. Direction des fibres, logique d'entrelacement, variation de couleur par fil, et passe normale micro-detail.\"\nsrc/projectSlides.jsx:3482:function HoudiniGameEnvSlides({ isMobile, lang }) {\nsrc/projectSlides.jsx:3492:          {imgZoom(\"fractal-voronoi.webp\", \"Houdini Game Environments\", { mask: \"left\", radius: 0 })}\nsrc/projectSlides.jsx:3494:        <h1 style={titleStyle}>{t(\"Houdini Game Environments\", \"Environnements Jeu Houdini\")}</h1>\nsrc/projectSlides.jsx:3496:          \"Deep dive into creating assets and architecture for game environments, from Maya and ZBrush to Unreal Engine 5. Procedural modeling HDAs focusing on orientation, alignment, and rapid variation. Houdini handles alignment through the normal attribute - no manual rotation needed.\",\nsrc/projectSlides.jsx:3497:          \"Plongee dans la creation d'assets et d'architecture pour les environnements de jeu. HDAs de modelisation procedurale axees sur l'orientation et l'alignement. Houdini gere l'alignement via l'attribut normal - pas de rotation manuelle.\"\nsrc/projectSlides.jsx:3505:        {h2(t(\"Procedural Walls\", \"Murs proceduraux\"))}\nsrc/projectSlides.jsx:3507:          {imgZoom(\"walls.webp\", \"Procedural Walls\", { mask: \"right\", radius: 0 })}\nsrc/projectSlides.jsx:3530:          {imgZoom(\"/procedural-environments-hero.webp\", \"Procedural Environments\", { mask: \"right\", radius: 0 })}\nsrc/projectSlides.jsx:3572:          \"Procedural planter modeled in Houdini. Quick variation of dimensions, material types, and ornamentation through parametric controls.\",\nsrc/projectSlides.jsx:3573:          \"Bac de fleurs procedural modelise dans Houdini. Variation rapide des dimensions, types de materiaux et ornementations via des controles parametriques.\"\nsrc/projectSlides.jsx:3750:        <h1 style={titleStyle}>{t(\"Procedural Water Wheel\", \"Roue a eau procedurale\")}</h1>\nsrc/projectSlides.jsx:3752:          \"I deconstructed and divided several modules to build this fully procedural waterwheel geometry in Houdini, before integrating a water simulation (FLIP). The objective: create a flexible system designed to evolve with production feedback. Turning technical complexity into an iterative creative tool. A huge thank you to David Silberbauer and Gnomon for this foundational workshop. Shared knowledge is an invaluable asset.\",\nsrc/projectSlides.jsx:3753:          \"J'ai deconstruit et divise plusieurs modules pour construire cette geometrie de roue a eau entierement procedurale dans Houdini, avant d'integrer une simulation d'eau (FLIP). L'objectif : creer un systeme flexible concu pour evoluer avec les retours de production. Un grand merci a David Silberbauer et Gnomon pour cet atelier fondateur.\"\nsrc/projectSlides.jsx:3809:          {imgZoom(\"slide1.webp\", \"Procedural Rock Gen\", { mask: \"right\" })}\nsrc/projectSlides.jsx:3811:        <h1 style={titleStyle}>{t(\"Procedural Rock Gen\", \"Generation de rochers procedurale\")}</h1>\nsrc/projectSlides.jsx:3840:function PampaGrassSlides2({ isMobile, lang }) {\nsrc/projectSlides.jsx:3850:          {imgZoom(\"thumbnail.webp\", \"Pampa Grass\", { mask: \"left\" })}\nsrc/projectSlides.jsx:3852:        <h1 style={titleStyle}>{t(\"Pampa Grass HDA\", \"Pampa Grass HDA\")}</h1>\nsrc/projectSlides.jsx:3865:          \"The HDA is divided into four modules: Fiber, Spine, Stems, and Grass. Every module shares attributes with the others. The Grass Scattering System shares the same logic as the Stems. VEX is the heart of this tool - it handles natural curls, noise-driven orientation, and attribute randomization.\",\nsrc/projectSlides.jsx:3871:            {captionBelow(t(\"Complete Pampa Grass HDA - infinite variations from one node\", \"HDA Pampa Grass complet - variations infinies a partir d'un noeud\"))}\n"},"started_at_ms":1789590918196,"completed_at_ms":1789590918196}}
